4.2 Citizenship and Ethnicity
4.2.1 Citizenship
Citizenship is the status of a person that is recognized by law as being a member of a country.
It is used to identify the population that is eligible for cert ain public services such as
employment, education and health services. Ugandans constituted 98.5 percent of the total
population as shown in table 4.2.

